    "spans": [
     {
      "end": 544,
      "start": 0,
      "text": "Juniper berry\nA juniper berry is the female seed cone produced by the various species of junipers . It is not a true berry but a cone with unusually fleshy and merged scales , which give it a berry-like appearance . The cones from a handful of species , especially Juniperus communis , are used as a spice , particularly in European cuisine , and also give gin its distinctive flavour . Juniper berries have been called the only spice derived from conifers , although tar and inner bark from pine trees is sometimes considered a spice as well ."
     }
